            <ArticleTitle>4-(Pyrrolidinyl)methoxybenzoic acid derivatives as a potent, orally active VLA-4 antagonist.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1515-29</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A novel series of benzoic acid derivatives as VLA-4 antagonists were synthesized. Optimization, focusing on activity and lipophilicity needed for cell permeability, resulted in the identification of 15b and 15e with good activity (IC50 = 1.6 nM each) and moderate lipophilicity (Log D = 2.0, 1.8). Furthermore, 15e demonstrated efficacy in murine asthma model by an oral dose of 30 mg/kg.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
